{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305126,"nonce":"G+42UsT+I79LI6ZjDUN9lRo+S5Y=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhfnA","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/9","origin":"github"},"title":"Any stat or read error aborts the entire run","message":"`get_possible_files()` calls `os.lstat(filepath)` on every file found during the walk with no error handling, and `check_file_chunk()` reads with none either.\n\nA broken symlink, a permission-denied directory, or an `EIO` from a failing sector terminates the whole scan — potentially hours in.\n\nThis tool exists to salvage data from disks that are incomplete or failing, so I/O errors are the expected case, not an exceptional one. They should mark the affected region as unknown and continue.\n\nRelated: the report should distinguish three states, which it currently conflates into two — verified, genuinely missing, and *unknown* (unreadable). Reporting an unreadable piece as \"missing\" is misleading when the disk is dying.","files":null}]}